Concept A is a prerequisite for concept B. And concept B is a prerequisite for concept

26:46.280 --> 26:46.600
C.

26:46.920 --> 26:47.780
A to B to C.

26:47.940 --> 26:48.200
Got it.

26:48.200 --> 26:50.660
And concept C is our ultimate target.

26:51.440 --> 26:56.860
Now, assume the curriculum graph also registers a loose topical similarity between concept

26:56.860 --> 26:58.260
A and concept C.

26:58.620 --> 26:58.760
Okay.

26:59.240 --> 27:04.220
On an undirected map, both A and B appear to be exactly one step away from the target

27:04.220 --> 27:10.140
C. The algorithm begins at C, looks for the nearest nodes, and might arbitrarily select

